<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Almaty</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Alma-Ata, Verny</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Almaty is the largest city of Kazakhstan, at the foot of the Trans-Ili Alatau mountains in the south-east of the country. Founded as the Russian fort of Verny in 1854, it was renamed Alma-Ata in 1921 and became capital of the Kazakh republic in 1929. It remained the capital of independent Kazakhstan until the government moved to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/astana">Astana</a> in 1997.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/almaty.jpg" alt="Almaty" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dauren Nabijan · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Almaty_K%C3%B6k_T%C3%B6be.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
